---
description: Typography, theme and security paths must not regress the design constraints; the security paths also need a human review
globs: ["packages/typeset/**", "packages/theme/**", "packages/core/src/sanitize/**", "apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json", "apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---
The sanitiser, `tauri.conf.json` and `capabilities/` are covered by CODEOWNERS: a human approves the PR (ADR-0028). Typography and theme paths merge on a signed review, so the constraints below are the whole check. Keep `docs/design-language.md` constraints intact (measure in ch, grid multiples from `--marxy-line-box`, hierarchy by size and weight only, chrome at rest zero). Any visual change needs before/after screenshots attached and a row in `docs/taste-review/queue.md`. Sanitising is never off; the CSP never gains an http(s) source; themes never get JavaScript or network access.
